 "_about": "Which standards GOVERN an equipment type (#725 F5, #733). Keys are the equipment types of reference/equipment_vocabulary.json (one vocabulary: subject_scope reads what a submittal is from it). A governing standard that the library holds is selected for a submittal of that type (method governing_standard, included) with the type and where it was read; one the library does not hold is listed as governing_not_held, never as met. materials_standards apply only to material fields of a datasheet (subject_scope.materials_gate). Generic engineering standards only; edit here, not in code. partial_standards: a standard an equipment type takes only IN PART (ASME VIII Div 1 governs a relief valve only through its pressure relief device rules): on a review of that type, only the standard's requirements whose own words name one of `words` are checks; the rest do not apply, with the reason (subject_scope.partial_gate). equipment_subtypes: for an equipment type whose standards each govern only some sub-types (API 610 centrifugal pumps, API 674 reciprocating pumps): `subtypes` = sub-type -> the words that state it on a datasheet; `standards` = standard -> the sub-types it governs. A standard whose sub-types the sheet does not state is asked of the engineer, one for another sub-type is not required (equipment_subtype.py).",
